  "step_1": "The decision reason considers the minimum probability of each lottery and prefers the lottery with the higher value of minimum probability. In this context, 'minimum probability' is ambiguous because both lotteries have only two outcomes (one non-zero loss and one zero outcome), so each lottery has a smallest (minimum) probability associated with the loss outcome. For Lottery A, the minimum probability is 0.1% (associated with the -6000 loss), and for Lottery B, it is 0.2% (associated with the -3000 loss). The decision reason would thus compare these two values: 0.1% vs. 0.2%. Since 0.2% > 0.1%, the reason would prefer Lottery B. Therefore, the decision reason can be applied to the decision problem, and it would lead to a preference for Lottery B based on having the higher minimum probability (0.2% > 0.1%).",
